[W15-E25] 🟧 Source coding redundancy for n=6 = log2(4/3) = GZ_WIDTH
  Shannon source coding for uniform n=6 symbol source:
    H = log2(6) = 2.584963 bits
    ceil(H) = 3 bits needed
    Redundancy = 3 - log2(6) = log2(8) - log2(6)
             = log2(8/6) = log2(1.3333)
             = log2(8/6) = log2(4/3) = GZ_WIDTH (in bits)!
    Exact match: True
    Redundancy = 0.415037
    GZ_
  UNIQUENESS: Exact! 3-log2(6)=log2(4/3)=GZ_WIDTH. Also holds for 12,24,48. Smallest is 6.

